+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` and answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`
+  (`dishes` is the number of dishes sold, the sum of `qty`). Tickets already
+  imported are skipped. A bad row answers `bad_request`; an item running out
+  answers `sale_out_of_stock` (409). Either way nothing is imported and the
+  message names the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers, per item,
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`, where
+  `difference` is `actual - theoretical`.
